<DocsLayout title="Reservations">
  <h1>Reservations</h1>
  <p>
    Reservations are for actions where cost is estimated before work starts,
    such as LLM token generation or long-running export jobs.
  </p>

  <h2>Reserve</h2>
  <p>
    <code>Reserve</code> consumes <code>reserve_cost</code> immediately and
    stores a reservation record containing the exact Redis keys touched.
  </p>

  <h2>Finalize</h2>
  <p>
    <code>FinalizeReservation</code> records actual cost. If actual cost is
    lower than reserved cost, refundable impacts are refunded. If actual cost
    is higher, overage is recorded but the original operation is not failed
    retroactively.
  </p>

  <h2>Release</h2>
  <p>
    <code>ReleaseReservation</code> is used when the operation definitely did
    not happen. Active refundable impacts are released idempotently.
  </p>

  <h2>Important invariant</h2>
  <p>
    Finalization and release use <code>ReservationImpact.redis_key</code>.
    They must not recompute the current window key from wall-clock time.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>

